---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
import DocCallout from "../../components/docs/DocCallout.astro"
import DocCode from "../../components/docs/DocCode.astro"

const toc = [
  { title: "Plugin Install", href: "#plugin-install", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Config Patching", href: "#config-patching", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Skills", href: "#skills", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Built-ins", href: "#built-ins", depth: 2 },
]
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Plugins & Skills"
  subtitle="Plugin loading and skill discovery from packages/nikcli/src/plugin and packages/nikcli/src/skill."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="plugin-install" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Plugin Install</h2>
    <p>
      <code>nikcli plugin &lt;module&gt;</code> installs a module, reads its manifest, and merges the
      plugin config into the chosen nikcli config file.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash">
      nikcli plugin my-nikcli-plugin
      nikcli plugin my-nikcli-plugin --global
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="config-patching" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Config Patching</h2>
    <p>
      The install flow can target project or global config, respects existing <code>nikcli.json</code>
      files, and supports forceful merge paths when a plugin needs to write overlapping config.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="skills" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Skills</h2>
    <p>
      Skills are discovered via <code>{`{skill,skills}`}</code> globs in config directories, plus
      <code>.claude/skills</code> and plugin-provided skill folders when available.
    </p>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Skill format">
      <p>
        Each skill requires a <code>SKILL.md</code> with frontmatter <code>name</code> and <code>description</code>.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="built-ins" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Built-ins</h2>
    <p>
      nikcli also ships built-in plugin behavior for core auth and runtime integrations. Set
      <code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_DEFAULT_PLUGINS</code> to skip those defaults when you need a tighter
      environment.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
